# M6 4c (slice 348; Codex CODEX-OPUS-348-ROUTE-B-REPLY-20261110T081925Z-01, CODEX-OPUS-348-LAYOUT-REPLY-20261110T083210Z-01):
# the named actual `p: y: int: 6` is a written Structure value; the lowering lays it out where it is written (the cell y
# holds 6) and the formal p receives that Structure by reference, reading its field y by role -- 62 exits 7.
Point:
    int: x 1
    int: y 2
end: Point
fn: take (Point: p; int: q 2) int
    return: p\y * 10 + q
end: take
int: code 7
if: take(p: y: int: 6) != 62
    code: 81
---
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: code; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
